<urn:usf:policy:provider-account-retry:1> <urn:usf:predicate:admissionRule> "Immediately before contact, under the selected source-key single-flight lock, authenticate and consume the complete current maximal selected-key deferral antichain. Every retained retryable head must have non-null retryAfter no later than contactAdmissionInstant; any later gate refuses without contact. A source-movement-required head has null retryAfter and blocks this exact key until relevant mapping/protocol/credential identity movement derives a different source key. Profile or authorization churn never bypasses a gate." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:policy:provider-account-retry:1> <urn:usf:predicate:attemptWindowMilliseconds> "3600000" <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:policy:provider-account-retry:1> <urn:usf:predicate:baseDelayMilliseconds> "30000" <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:policy:provider-account-retry:1> <urn:usf:predicate:chainRule> "After settlement derive attemptWindowDigest from the source key, exact retry-policy semantic digest and settlement-derived window bounds. previousAttemptDigests is the sorted unique zero-through-32 antichain of every consumed maximal same-key attempt whose attemptWindowDigest equals that settlement window. attemptOrdinal is one plus the cardinality of their bounded unique transitive same-window attempt-event union; an empty predecessor set is permitted only for ordinal one. Consumed prior-window heads gate admission but are not predecessors in the new window. Cycles, missing, ancestor-retaining, skipped, over-bound, cross-key/window or policy-mismatched retry DAGs refuse." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:policy:provider-account-retry:1> <urn:usf:predicate:delayRule> "For retryable attemptOrdinal n in 1..5, delayMilliseconds=min(900000,30000*2^(n-1)+jitterMilliseconds). retryAfter=attemptedAt+delay except the fifth attempt sets disposition circuit-open and retryAfter=max(attemptedAt+delay,windowExpiresAt). Arithmetic uses exact safe integers and overflow refuses." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:policy:provider-account-retry:1> <urn:usf:predicate:jitterMaximumMilliseconds> "10000" <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:policy:provider-account-retry:1> <urn:usf:predicate:jitterRule> "jitterMilliseconds is the unsigned big-endian first four bytes of SHA-256 over USF canonical JSON v1 [accountSourceKeyDigest,windowStartedAt,attemptOrdinal], modulo 10001." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
