<urn:usf:policy:provider-account-retry:1> <urn:usf:predicate:resetRule> "A successful current observation supersedes consumed failure heads for that source. A settlement-derived new window starts at ordinal one only after every consumed prior-window retryAfter has elapsed at admission; this covers ordinary and circuit-open retries and contact crossing a window boundary. The head-set update removes exactly the consumed prior-window heads and retains any newly concurrent incomparable heads. Authorization/profile churn cannot reset or bypass the source-local gate, while relevant source-key movement creates a different independent key." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
