<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:concurrencyRule> "Different accountSourceKeyDigests may acquire concurrently from the same immutable base and materialize branch heads. One source-key-specific single-flight lock at .usf/locks/provider-account-source-{accountSourceKeyDigest}.lock spans its authoritative contact or local identity refresh through no-replace successor materialization, so new same-key work joins or reuses that exact result and never blocks another key. The lock is one persistent invoking-uid-owned regular non-symlink mode-0600 nlink-1 inode opened no-follow beneath the authenticated mode-0700 .usf/locks directory and is never replaced while waiters may exist. Merge/successor computation holds no provider, Git or primary-mutation lock. Same-source branches already produced by crash or older writers may be reconciled only through fresh-authority selected-source acquire; verify refuses a selected-key conflict, while reduce retains it as an explicit bounded revision antichain and unrelated keys remain schedulable." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:effectiveStateRule> "Each manifest is a complete multi-version snapshot with one bounded effective source-revision antichain per sourceKind plus accountSourceKeyDigest. Across supplied post-checkpoint parent closures, identical revisions deduplicate and a revision supersedes another only when every traversed previousSourceRevisionDigests link is present and authenticated in that closure. A checkpoint's retained effective members are new comparison roots without changing their factual/revision bytes; predecessor links leaving the checkpoint are opaque and never prove ancestry. Missing, pruned or pre-checkpoint-only ancestry is unknown and therefore incomparable, not an error or ancestor. Different effective revisions for one key with neither proven ancestral to the other are all retained as explicit concurrent conflict. No preference winner is selected, and conflict for one key does not prevent unrelated keys from advancing or being reduced." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
