<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:headSetDeferralCapacityRule> "Before contact admission, canonicalize and authenticate the current deferral antichain and require capacity to persist either one new selected-key attempt after replacing its exact consumed heads or, for a previously undeferred key, one additional entry within the 512-entry bound. A full unrelated-key deferral set refuses before credentials are consumed or contact begins; no entry is evicted, sampled or preference-selected. A selected key may join at most 32 same-window incomparable retry heads in one bounded attempt, after which those exact heads become ancestors of the single returned attempt." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:provider-operation:source-state-manifest:1> <urn:usf:predicate:headSetDeferralRule> "For each source key, authenticate the exact deferral heads consumed at contact admission. On settlement, CAS removes only those consumed selected-key heads and adds a returned failed attempt; within one window its previousAttemptDigests join every consumed maximal retry head, while a new policy-derived window starts a new retry DAG after the expired consumed heads are removed. Authenticate and prune only attempt heads proven by bounded retry-DAG ancestry, and retain every newly concurrent incomparable head on compare-and-swap mismatch. A successful selected-source observation or host identity removes only its consumed deferrals and adds none. Unrelated-key deferrals are byte-identical. A failed conflict reconciliation therefore survives process restart without pretending to be a factual manifest successor." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
