<urn:usf:requirement:operator-provider-command-reservation:2> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "The predecessor-owned static operator registry reserves the complete graph-known providers command tree exactly once: census, status, aliases, host census, account-source receipt acquire, verify and pure reduce, plus bounded receipt projection list; static doctor/provider-home and receipt account-source; explicit frozen catalogue digests; explicit protocol-scoped source-state head-set record and bounded manifest heads; owner-private selected env-file and bounded credential-source selection file, host-census, route-narrowing and projection pagination help. It owns src/commands/providers.ts and one decomposed src/commands/provider-leaf-dispatch.ts boundary. Module presence and parent-process importability are never authority. Each production leaf invocation must use one fresh single-invocation Node child; the long-running parent may not import or cache a feature handler. The parent binds the selected root to its implementation root and holds the shared primary-mutation lock before the child's first repository-module load. In that fresh process the child rederives the exact explicit profile/manifest owner, current verified completion and current file-based basis, selects the unique typed ProductionLeafRuntimeClosure, canonicalizes identical path/digest rows into sorted roles, refuses missing members, conflicting digests or unknown roles, authenticates every same-root regular non-symlink member by SHA-256, imports only the declared handler and reauthenticates the entry bytes. The child then releases its shared lock and emits one bounded prepared message; the parent releases its shared lock and acknowledges; only after that acknowledgement may the handler or provider inference begin. Use exact process.execPath without a shell, scrub inherited credentials, proxies and Node mutation options, bound the control/result protocol, and allow no same-process or alternate-route fallback. Failure before or after preparation terminates the child and returns one stable refusal. Concurrent children and readers remain parallel; only cooperative primary mutation takes the exclusive lock, and inference never holds it. Confined validation uses injected authority, lock, loader and child-handshake substitutes with no real child or provider contact, including one planted shared/preloaded-module movement case. Feature packets implement only their leaf modules and never rewrite the predecessor registry, dispatcher, help, CLI or child boundary. Git and GitHub state are not authority." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
